{
  "schema_version": "3.0",
  "key": "causative_constructions",
  "concept_slug": "causative_constructions",
  "grounding_mode": "fallback_no_wiki",
  "title": "Making, Letting, and Getting Someone to Do Something",
  "cefr_level": "B1",
  "goal": "Use common Bokmål causative patterns with an object plus infinitive or adjective.",
  "elements": [
    {
      "kind": "section",
      "role": "orient",
      "title": "What causatives do",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "kind": "paragraph",
          "spans": [
            {
              "kind": "text",
              "value": "A causative construction is a pattern that says one person or situation causes another person or thing to do something, be allowed to do something, or become something. In Norwegian, you often build this with a verb like "
            },
            {
              "kind": "foreign_term",
              "value": "få",
              "lang": "no"
            },
            {
              "kind": "text",
              "value": ", "
            },
            {
              "kind": "foreign_term",
              "value": "la",
              "lang": "no"
            },
            {
              "kind": "text",
              "value": ", or "
            },
            {
              "kind": "foreign_term",
              "value": "gjøre",
              "lang": "no"
            },
            {
              "kind": "text",
              "value": "."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "kind": "rule",
          "statement": [
            {
              "kind": "text",
              "value": "Use causative patterns when English has meanings like get someone to do, let someone do, make someone do, or make someone adjective."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "kind": "example",
          "no": [
            {
              "kind": "text",
              "value": "Læreren fikk studentene til å snakke norsk."
            }
          ],
          "en": [
            {
              "kind": "text",
              "value": "The teacher got the students to speak Norwegian."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "kind": "example",
          "no": [
            {
              "kind": "text",
              "value": "Hun lot barna se filmen."
            }
          ],
          "en": [
            {
              "kind": "text",
              "value": "She let the children watch the film."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "kind": "example",
          "no": [
            {
              "kind": "text",
              "value": "Nyheten gjorde ham glad."
            }
          ],
          "en": [
            {
              "kind": "text",
              "value": "The news made him happy."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "kind": "section",
      "role": "model",
      "title": "Get someone to do something",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "kind": "paragraph",
          "spans": [
            {
              "kind": "text",
              "value": "Use "
            },
            {
              "kind": "foreign_term",
              "value": "få",
              "lang": "no"
            },
            {
              "kind": "text",
              "value": " with an object, the affected person or thing, plus "
            },
            {
              "kind": "foreign_term",
              "value": "til å",
              "lang": "no"
            },
            {
              "kind": "text",
              "value": " and an infinitive, the base form of a verb with "
            },
            {
              "kind": "foreign_term",
              "value": "å",
              "lang": "no"
            },
            {
              "kind": "text",
              "value": ". This pattern means that someone persuades, arranges, or manages to make another person do an action."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "kind": "rule",
          "statement": [
            {
              "kind": "foreign_term",
              "value": "få noen til å",
              "lang": "no"
            },
            {
              "kind": "text",
              "value": " + infinitive means get someone to do something."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "kind": "example",
          "no": [
            {
              "kind": "text",
              "value": "Jeg prøver å få noen til å bytte vakt med meg."
            }
          ],
          "en": [
            {
              "kind": "text",
              "value": "I am trying to get someone to swap shifts with me."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "kind": "example",
          "no": [
            {
              "kind": "text",
              "value": "Sjefen fikk oss til å jobbe overtid."
            }
          ],
          "en": [
            {
              "kind": "text",
              "value": "The boss got us to work overtime."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "kind": "callout",
          "level": "tip",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "kind": "paragraph",
              "spans": [
                {
                  "kind": "text",
                  "value": "The person who does the action comes between "
                },
                {
                  "kind": "foreign_term",
                  "value": "få",
                  "lang": "no"
                },
                {
                  "kind": "text",
                  "value": " and "
                },
                {
                  "kind": "foreign_term",
                  "value": "til å",
                  "lang": "no"
                },
                {
                  "kind": "text",
                  "value": ". Keep the infinitive after "
                },
                {
                  "kind": "foreign_term",
                  "value": "til å",
                  "lang": "no"
                },
                {
                  "kind": "text",
                  "value": "."
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "kind": "exercise",
      "id": "ex_choose_fa",
      "operation": "choose",
      "prompt": [
        {
          "kind": "text",
          "value": "Choose the pattern that means “get someone to do something.”"
        }
      ],
      "explanation": [
        {
          "kind": "text",
          "value": "Correct. "
        },
        {
          "kind": "foreign_term",
          "value": "få noen til å",
          "lang": "no"
        },
        {
          "kind": "text",
          "value": " takes an object and then an infinitive action."
        }
      ],
      "payload": {
        "options": [
          {
            "option_id": "a",
            "text": "få noen til å",
            "why": "This means get someone to do something."
          },
          {
            "option_id": "b",
            "text": "la noen",
            "why": "This means let or allow someone."
          },
          {
            "option_id": "c",
            "text": "gjøre noen",
            "why": "This is used with an adjective to mean make someone become something."
          }
        ],
        "answer_id": "a",
        "stem": [
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": "Which phrase fits this meaning?"
          }
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "kind": "exercise",
      "id": "ex_fill_fa",
      "operation": "recall_fill",
      "prompt": [
        {
          "kind": "text",
          "value": "Complete the sentence with the right causative phrase."
        }
      ],
      "explanation": [
        {
          "kind": "text",
          "value": "Yes. The sentence needs "
        },
        {
          "kind": "foreign_term",
          "value": "fikk oss til å",
          "lang": "no"
        },
        {
          "kind": "text",
          "value": " because we were caused to do the action."
        }
      ],
      "payload": {
        "segments": [
          {
            "kind": "span",
            "spans": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "Kurset "
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "kind": "blank",
            "blank_id": "b1",
            "options": [
              "fikk oss til å",
              "lot oss",
              "gjorde oss"
            ],
            "answer_index": 0
          },
          {
            "kind": "span",
            "spans": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": " tenke på en ny måte."
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "kind": "section",
      "role": "contrast",
      "title": "Let someone do something",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "kind": "paragraph",
          "spans": [
            {
              "kind": "text",
              "value": "Use "
            },
            {
              "kind": "foreign_term",
              "value": "la",
              "lang": "no"
            },
            {
              "kind": "text",
              "value": " when the subject allows an action instead of causing it by pressure or persuasion. The verb after the object is a bare infinitive, the base verb without "
            },
            {
              "kind": "foreign_term",
              "value": "å",
              "lang": "no"
            },
            {
              "kind": "text",
              "value": "."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "kind": "rule",
          "statement": [
            {
              "kind": "foreign_term",
              "value": "la noen",
              "lang": "no"
            },
            {
              "kind": "text",
              "value": " + bare infinitive means let someone do something."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "kind": "example",
          "no": [
            {
              "kind": "text",
              "value": "De lot meg låne bilen."
            }
          ],
          "en": [
            {
              "kind": "text",
              "value": "They let me borrow the car."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "kind": "example",
          "no": [
            {
              "kind": "text",
              "value": "Vi lar barna velge selv."
            }
          ],
          "en": [
            {
              "kind": "text",
              "value": "We let the children choose for themselves."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "kind": "callout",
          "level": "warning",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "kind": "paragraph",
              "spans": [
                {
                  "kind": "text",
                  "value": "Do not add "
                },
                {
                  "kind": "foreign_term",
                  "value": "å",
                  "lang": "no"
                },
                {
                  "kind": "text",
                  "value": " after the object with "
                },
                {
                  "kind": "foreign_term",
                  "value": "la",
                  "lang": "no"
                },
                {
                  "kind": "text",
                  "value": ". Say "
                },
                {
                  "kind": "foreign_term",
                  "value": "lot meg låne",
                  "lang": "no"
                },
                {
                  "kind": "text",
                  "value": ", not "
                },
                {
                  "kind": "foreign_term",
                  "value": "lot meg å låne",
                  "lang": "no"
                },
                {
                  "kind": "text",
                  "value": "."
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "kind": "exercise",
      "id": "ex_judge_la",
      "operation": "judge",
      "prompt": [
        {
          "kind": "text",
          "value": "Decide whether the sentence uses "
        },
        {
          "kind": "foreign_term",
          "value": "la",
          "lang": "no"
        },
        {
          "kind": "text",
          "value": " correctly."
        }
      ],
      "explanation": [
        {
          "kind": "text",
          "value": "Right. After "
        },
        {
          "kind": "foreign_term",
          "value": "la",
          "lang": "no"
        },
        {
          "kind": "text",
          "value": " plus object, Norwegian uses the bare infinitive without "
        },
        {
          "kind": "foreign_term",
          "value": "å",
          "lang": "no"
        },
        {
          "kind": "text",
          "value": "."
        }
      ],
      "payload": {
        "sentence": [
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": "Hun lot meg å prøve igjen."
          }
        ],
        "is_correct": false,
        "feedback": "Use lot meg prøve, without å."
      }
    },
    {
      "kind": "exercise",
      "id": "ex_find_fix_la",
      "operation": "find_fix",
      "prompt": [
        {
          "kind": "text",
          "value": "Find the token that makes the sentence incorrect."
        }
      ],
      "explanation": [
        {
          "kind": "text",
          "value": "Correct. "
        },
        {
          "kind": "foreign_term",
          "value": "La",
          "lang": "no"
        },
        {
          "kind": "text",
          "value": " takes a bare infinitive after the object."
        }
      ],
      "payload": {
        "tokens": [
          {
            "token_id": "t1",
            "text": "Vi"
          },
          {
            "token_id": "t2",
            "text": "lot"
          },
          {
            "token_id": "t3",
            "text": "dem"
          },
          {
            "token_id": "t4",
            "text": "å"
          },
          {
            "token_id": "t5",
            "text": "vente"
          },
          {
            "token_id": "t6",
            "text": "inne"
          }
        ],
        "error_token_id": "t4",
        "feedback": "Remove å: Vi lot dem vente inne."
      }
    },
    {
      "kind": "section",
      "role": "model",
      "title": "Make someone become something",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "kind": "paragraph",
          "spans": [
            {
              "kind": "text",
              "value": "Use "
            },
            {
              "kind": "foreign_term",
              "value": "gjøre",
              "lang": "no"
            },
            {
              "kind": "text",
              "value": " when the result is a state or quality. The word after the object is often an adjective such as happy, tired, or nervous."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "kind": "rule",
          "statement": [
            {
              "kind": "foreign_term",
              "value": "gjøre noen",
              "lang": "no"
            },
            {
              "kind": "text",
              "value": " + adjective means make someone become that way."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "kind": "example",
          "no": [
            {
              "kind": "text",
              "value": "Musikken gjorde henne rolig."
            }
          ],
          "en": [
            {
              "kind": "text",
              "value": "The music made her calm."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "kind": "example",
          "no": [
            {
              "kind": "text",
              "value": "Alt arbeidet gjorde oss slitne."
            }
          ],
          "en": [
            {
              "kind": "text",
              "value": "All the work made us tired."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "kind": "paragraph",
          "spans": [
            {
              "kind": "text",
              "value": "With plural objects, ordinary adjective agreement can appear, as in "
            },
            {
              "kind": "foreign_term",
              "value": "oss slitne",
              "lang": "no"
            },
            {
              "kind": "text",
              "value": ". The causative pattern itself is still "
            },
            {
              "kind": "foreign_term",
              "value": "gjøre",
              "lang": "no"
            },
            {
              "kind": "text",
              "value": " plus object plus result."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
